"""The mutants of the capacity probe's own part. Each row: (name, 'op', exact anchor, replacement). The anchor must occur
exactly once in the built source and be a text of op.py (mutate.py check). One mutant per constant the signers rely
on, per member of effects_of(), per need() of validate_plan and of the precheck, per clause of the grammar of each
line, per branch of the verdict after the containers, per member of the receipt; and, for the pinned scripts, one
mutant per behaviour their tests must see.

A mutant of a script (prefix S) replaces the whole constant (CALENDAR_SCRIPT, IDENT_SCRIPT or LOAD_SCRIPT) together
with its SHA-256 and size, recomputed here from the mutated text: the source then gives the container the mutated
bytes as its own pinned ones, and only a test that RUNS the script (tests/test_scripts.py, tests/test_native.py) or
reads its constants (tests/test_probe.py) can kill it."""
import hashlib
from pathlib import Path
import re

MUTANTS=[]
COMBOS={}
REDUNDANT={}
def add(name,old,new):MUTANTS.append((name,'op',old,new))

OWN=(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent/'op.py').read_text()
def script(name,constant,old,new):
    begin=constant+"_SCRIPT=r'''";start=OWN.index(begin);stop=OWN.index('\n',OWN.index(constant+'_SCRIPT_BYTES='))+1
    block=OWN[start:stop];text=block[len(begin):block.index("'''\n"+constant+"_SCRIPT_SHA256=")]
    assert text.count(old)==1,(name,text.count(old))
    changed=text.replace(old,new);raw=changed.encode('ascii')
    add(name,block,"%s%s'''\n%s_SCRIPT_SHA256='%s'\n%s_SCRIPT_BYTES=%d\n"%(begin,changed,constant,hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest(),constant,len(raw)))

